 ![Debug Contracts tab](https://github.com/scaffold-eth/scaffold-eth-2/assets/55535804/b237af0c-5027-4849-a5c1-2e31495cccb1)
 
+## USDC staking dApp
+
+This repo is a USDC staking app built on Scaffold-ETH 2 and targeting **Base**.
+
+- `packages/hardhat/contracts/Staker.sol` — a minimal vault: `stake(amount)`, `withdraw(amount)`,
+  `withdrawAll()`. No rewards, no fees, no owner, not upgradeable. Your position is always exactly
+  what you put in, and only you can move it.
+- `packages/hardhat/contracts/MockUSDC.sol` — local stand-in for USDC (same name, symbol and
+  6 decimals). Deployed on local chains only; `mint` is open so any dev account can fund itself.
+- `packages/nextjs/app/stake` — the `/stake` page: stake, withdraw, and see your wallet USDC
+  balance, your gas (ETH) balance and your staked position.
+
+Token addresses used by `packages/hardhat/deploy/01_deploy_staker.ts`:
+
+| Network         | USDC                                         |
+| --------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
+| Base (8453)     | `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913` |
+| Base Sepolia    | `0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e` |
+| Local (31337)   | `MockUSDC`, deployed as `USDC`               |
+
+Deploying to any other chain fails on purpose — pointing the vault at the wrong token is
+unrecoverable.
+
+### Local development
+
+```bash
+yarn chain     # terminal 1
+yarn deploy    # terminal 2 — deploys MockUSDC (as "USDC") + Staker, mints 1M mock USDC to the deployer
+yarn start     # terminal 3 — http://localhost:3000/stake
+yarn test      # Staker unit tests
+```
+
+To fund another local account with mock USDC, call `USDC.mint` from the **Debug Contracts** page.
+
+Because `scaffold.config.ts` targets Base alongside hardhat, SE-2 hides the burner wallet
+(`burnerWalletMode: "localNetworksOnly"`). For burner-based local testing, temporarily drop
+`chains.base` from `targetNetworks`.
+
+### Deploying to Base
+
+```bash
+yarn account:import                # or `yarn generate` for a fresh deployer
+yarn deploy --network base
+yarn verify --network base
+```
+
+`yarn deploy` regenerates `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts`, which is what the
+frontend reads. Once the Staker is live on Base, set `targetNetworks: [chains.base]` in
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts` so the app stops offering the local chain.
+
+### Notes on the UI
+
+- Staking is two transactions (ERC20 `approve`, then `stake`); both steps are shown up front and
+  the approval is for exactly the amount being staked.
+- Amounts are parsed at 6 decimals and displayed truncated, never rounded up, so a shown balance
+  is always spendable.
+- Withdrawing the full position calls `withdrawAll()` instead of `withdraw(balance)`, so a balance
+  that moved between reading and sending can't leave dust behind.
+- The page warns when the ETH balance is too low to pay for gas, and blocks staking when the
+  wallet is on a network where the vault isn't deployed.
+
 ## Requirements
 
 Before you begin, you need to install the following tools:
